WEBVTT

00:05:57.926 --> 00:06:00.525
We all hate the feeling of missing out.

00:06:00.549 --> 00:06:02.601
So, actually, there was
this recent lottery,

00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:04.131
a mega-jackpot lottery,

00:06:04.155 --> 00:06:07.105
that had a huge payoff,
something like over a billion dollars.

00:06:07.129 --> 00:06:10.308
And everyone in my office
is pooling money to buy lottery tickets,

00:06:10.332 --> 00:06:11.973
and I'm not having any of this.

00:06:11.997 --> 00:06:14.247
There I am, like, swaggering
around the office,

00:06:14.271 --> 00:06:17.110
"Lotteries are a special tax
on people who can't do math."

00:06:17.134 --> 00:06:18.187
(Laughter)

00:06:18.211 --> 00:06:19.523
And then it hits me:

00:06:19.973 --> 00:06:21.225
uh oh.

00:06:21.249 --> 00:06:22.598
What if they win?

00:06:22.622 --> 00:06:24.717
(Laughter)

00:06:24.741 --> 00:06:27.166
I'm the only one who shows up
at work the next day.

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:28.348
(Laughter)

00:06:28.372 --> 00:06:30.916
Now, it's not that I didn't want
my colleagues to win.